天哪，你还有写日记的习惯？

1096
00:48:01.790 --> 00:48:03.650
What am I doing with my life?
我这辈子都在干什么啊？

1097
00:48:03.770 --> 00:48:04.870
Does she have a journal?
她真的有写日记吗？

1098
00:48:05.110 --> 00:48:09.930
Let me show you what my mic sits on so I can reach it because I'm shorty.
让我给你们看看我的麦克风垫着什么，这样我才够得着，因为我个子矮。

1099
00:48:11.110 --> 00:48:12.170
Like seven journals.
大概有七本吧。

1100
00:48:13.470 --> 00:48:15.170
Like Holly Hobby on the front.
封面上还有霍莉·霍比的那种。

1101
00:48:15.650 --> 00:48:17.910
John, that's who I was.
约翰，我以前就是那样的人。

1102
00:48:17.910 --> 00:48:19.010
I mean, come on.
我是说，拜托。

1103
00:48:19.230 --> 00:48:19.530
Oh my God.
天哪。

1104
00:48:19.910 --> 00:48:21.090
Wait, who you were?
等等，你以前是什么样的人？

1105
00:48:21.330 --> 00:48:23.970
That seems like a current journal that is being written about right now.
那看起来像是现在正在写的日记。

1106
00:48:24.430 --> 00:48:25.550
I'm writing right now.
我正在写呢。

1107
00:48:26.130 --> 00:48:31.530
By the way, speaking of Polly Pocket or whatever, Holly Hobby, either one of those E's.
顺便说一下，说到Polly Pocket或者Holly Hobby，反正就是那两个带E结尾的名字。

1108
00:48:31.830 --> 00:48:34.410
It made me think of that kid sister thing before I signed on.
在我签约之前，这让我想起了那个“小妹妹”的梗。

1109
00:48:34.450 --> 00:48:37.850
I was like, I had all these like sputtering memories that were like, remember this?
当时我就想，我脑子里冒出了一堆零星的记忆，就像在说，还记得这个吗？

1110
00:48:37.950 --> 00:48:39.410
And I blacked out for about 20 minutes.
然后我断片了大概20分钟。

1111
00:48:39.890 --> 00:48:44.690
Okay, so I told on the podcast that we would do bits between scenes, kind of keep us going,
好的，我在播客里说过，我们会在拍摄间隙玩些梗，算是让我们保持状态，

1112
00:48:44.810 --> 00:48:46.410
that you really kept us all going.
是你真的让我们大家都保持了状态。

1113
00:48:46.610 --> 00:48:47.110
You really did.
你真的做到了。

1114
00:48:47.250 --> 00:48:50.230
And then I said, we would do this kid sister, big brother bit.
然后我说，我们要玩那个“小妹妹”和“大哥哥”的梗。

1115
00:48:50.370 --> 00:48:52.830
And Jenna was like, wait, what, where did that come from?
珍娜当时就说，等等，什么，那是什么梗？

1116
00:48:52.990 --> 00:48:53.530
What was that about?
那是怎么回事？

1117
00:48:53.530 --> 00:48:55.510
You're like, 1983 is where it came from.
你说，那是1983年的梗。

1118
00:48:58.140 --> 00:49:01.400
John, wasn't it because there was like a doll that was about my height?
约翰，难道不是因为当时有个跟我差不多高的玩偶吗？

1119
00:49:02.120 --> 00:49:04.880
Oh no, you were the identical replica of kid sister.
哦不，你简直就是“小妹妹”玩偶的复刻版。

1120
00:49:05.320 --> 00:49:09.060
And they had, it was, um, uh, kid, was it big brother?
他们当时有，嗯，呃，小妹妹，还有大哥哥吗？

1121
00:49:09.360 --> 00:49:10.700
No, no, something.
不，不，是别的什么。

1122
00:49:11.080 --> 00:49:14.040
I would go, you, I would yell around the corner.
我会走过去，你，我会从拐角处大喊。

1123
00:49:14.040 --> 00:49:15.240
No, there was a boy one.
不，有一个男孩款的。

1124
00:49:15.380 --> 00:49:16.580
And then they came out with a girl one.
然后他们又出了一个女孩款的。

1125
00:49:16.700 --> 00:49:18.120
It looked exactly like you.
长得跟你一模一样。

1126
00:49:18.920 --> 00:49:23.300
And I was at a store one day and saw it on a toy store, like shelf.
有一天我在商店里，在玩具店的货架上看到了它。

1127
00:49:23.440 --> 00:49:26.220
And I took a photo of myself standing next to it and I sent it to you.
我拍了一张自己站在它旁边的照片发给了你。

1128
00:49:26.380 --> 00:49:27.140
You were like, oh my God.
你当时说，天哪。

1129
00:49:27.140 --> 00:49:27.900
Oh, I remember that.
哦，我记得那个。

1130
00:49:28.080 --> 00:49:28.340
Yes.
是的。

1131
00:49:28.840 --> 00:49:33.080
But also you're the exact size of it compared to me, especially you're like the perfect.
而且你和它相比，大小也完全一样，尤其是你简直太完美了。

1132
00:49:33.080 --> 00:49:33.160
Perfect.
完美。

1133
00:49:33.620 --> 00:49:36.840
And I remember one day, didn't you do like the, the stiff arms and stuff?
我还记得有一天，你是不是做了那种僵硬的手臂动作之类的？

1134
00:49:37.000 --> 00:49:39.920
And I like picked you up and you were like, yeah, it was great.
然后我把你抱起来，你当时说，耶，太棒了。

1135
00:49:40.080 --> 00:49:40.700
It was good times.
那真是段好时光。

1136
00:49:40.940 --> 00:49:46.280
Someone, a fan wrote in and said, if you ever came on, could you and I, um, do the bit?
有人，有个粉丝写信来说，如果你来了，能不能和我一起表演那个梗？

1137
00:49:46.380 --> 00:49:48.280
And I was like, well, I, it's pretty.
我当时想，嗯，我，这挺……

1138
00:49:48.300 --> 00:49:48.920
Kid sister.
小妹妹。

1139
00:49:49.380 --> 00:49:50.160
Big brother.
大哥哥。

1140
00:49:50.560 --> 00:49:52.040
Oh, there it is.
哦，就是这个。

1141
00:49:52.900 --> 00:49:53.880
There it is.
就是这个。

1142
00:49:54.180 --> 00:49:55.540
Jenna, what jokes did we have?
珍娜，我们以前有什么笑话梗？

1143
00:49:55.640 --> 00:49:56.600
We didn't get along well.
我们以前相处得不太好。

1144
00:49:56.800 --> 00:49:58.120
What, what, what was it for us?
什么，什么，我们之间有什么梗？

1145
00:49:58.420 --> 00:49:59.160
Oh boy.
天哪。

1146
00:49:59.160 --> 00:49:59.700
Oh boy.
天哪。

1147
00:49:59.980 --> 00:50:01.020
What were our bits?
我们以前有什么梗？

1148
00:50:01.440 --> 00:50:02.440
What were our bits?
我们以前有什么梗？

1149
00:50:02.440 --> 00:50:02.960
Did we have bits?
我们有梗吗？

1150
00:50:02.960 --> 00:50:03.920
Boy, we had so many bits.
天哪，我们有太多梗了。

1151
00:50:04.120 --> 00:50:10.200
You know what I remember bits wise was many different, um, inside jokes of like writing
你知道我记得关于比特（bits）的事情，就是有很多不同的，嗯，关于写作的内部笑话，

1152
00:50:10.200 --> 00:50:15.540
on post-it notes and like all my memos that I had to hand to you for corporate always had
写在便利贴上，我所有必须交给你的公司备忘录上，总是

1153
00:50:15.540 --> 00:50:16.520
something written on them.
写着些什么。

1154
00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:22.200
John, you played one prank on me in the whole nine years of the office.
约翰，在《办公室》这九年里，你只对我搞过一次恶作剧。

1155
00:50:22.320 --> 00:50:26.360
Like one, like really fully formed, good, thought out prank.
就一次，那种真正完整、精彩、深思熟虑的恶作剧。

1156
00:50:26.360 --> 00:50:33.140
It was at Shroot Farms and you and I had this scene where we had to drive up to the farmhouse
那是在施鲁特农场，你和我有一场戏，我们得开车去农舍

1157
00:50:33.140 --> 00:50:42.060
several times and we're doing it and I am getting increasingly more hot.
好几次，我们拍着拍着，我感觉越来越热。

1158
00:50:42.060 --> 00:50:43.120
I'm like warm.
我感觉有点热。

1159
00:50:43.480 --> 00:50:44.280
I'm sweating.
我在出汗。

1160
00:50:44.700 --> 00:50:47.740
I'm like, oh my God, I'm like, it was so hot.
我心想，天哪，我心想，真是太热了。

1161
00:50:47.920 --> 00:50:53.100
And we had to turn off the AC for sound and you were like, yeah, I don't know.
为了收音我们得关掉空调，你说，是啊，我不知道。

1162
00:50:53.240 --> 00:50:54.960
I'm okay, but you're hot, huh?
我还好，但你很热，是吧？

1163
00:50:55.080 --> 00:50:57.280
And I'm like, I'm so hot.
我说，我真的太热了。

1164
00:50:57.680 --> 00:50:59.160
This went on for like 15 minutes.
这种情况持续了大约15分钟。

1165
00:50:59.160 --> 00:51:06.260
And then all of a sudden you start snickering and you had turned on my seat warmer all the
然后突然间你开始窃笑，原来你把我的座椅加热器开到了

1166
00:51:06.260 --> 00:51:08.260
way to the hottest setting.
最高档位。

1167
00:51:08.760 --> 00:51:09.440
Oh my God.
天哪。

1168
00:51:09.520 --> 00:51:10.840
That was late in the run, wasn't it?
那是剧集后期才发生的，对吧？

1169
00:51:10.940 --> 00:51:12.240
That was late in the run.
那是后期才发生的。

1170
00:51:12.420 --> 00:51:16.640
And I, but I was so excited because whenever we would go on talk shows, they would always
我当时特别兴奋，因为每当我们上脱口秀节目时，他们总会

1171
00:51:16.640 --> 00:51:19.120
ask us if we played pranks on each other.
问我们是否会互相搞恶作剧。

1172
00:51:19.200 --> 00:51:20.920
And I would always say no.
我总是说没有。

1173
00:51:21.100 --> 00:51:22.000
And I mean, not really.
我是说，真的没有。

1174
00:51:22.140 --> 00:51:27.540
I mean, besides just like little jokes on post-it notes or something, not really.
我的意思是，除了便利贴上的小笑话之类的，真的没有。

1175
00:51:28.380 --> 00:51:33.460
We weren't pranky, you know, but then finally, after you did that in the car, I was like,
我们不爱搞恶作剧，你知道的，但最后，在你车里搞了那次之后，我心想，

1176
00:51:33.580 --> 00:51:34.820
oh my gosh, this is great.
天哪，这太棒了。

1177
00:51:35.100 --> 00:51:38.240
I can finally have a prank to talk about.
我终于有一个恶作剧可以拿出来说了。

1178
00:51:39.380 --> 00:51:41.060
And you know what's sad about that prank?
你知道那个恶作剧有什么可悲的地方吗？

1179
00:51:41.240 --> 00:51:42.560
What's sad about that prank?
那个恶作剧有什么可悲的？

1180
00:51:42.580 --> 00:51:49.260
I realized that I'm such a bad prankster that I stole that prank from Clooney when we were
我意识到我是一个多么糟糕的恶作剧者，因为那个恶作剧是我在拍

1181
00:51:49.260 --> 00:51:50.020
doing Leatherheads.
《爱情达阵》时从克鲁尼那儿偷来的。

1182
00:51:50.220 --> 00:51:51.280
He did that to me.
他当时就是这么对我做的。

1183
00:51:51.700 --> 00:51:53.800
So that's how unoriginal I am.
所以我就是这么缺乏原创性。

1184
00:51:53.800 --> 00:51:57.500
I was like, I'm going to take George Clooney's band and do it to Jenna.
我当时心想，我要拿乔治·克鲁尼的招数来对付珍娜。

1185
00:51:57.780 --> 00:51:59.200
And I thought that would make me cool.
我还以为这会让我显得很酷。

1186
00:51:59.460 --> 00:51:59.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1187
00:51:59.680 --> 00:52:01.000
So basically, you're that.
所以基本上，你就是那样。

1188
00:52:01.300 --> 00:52:03.900
You got, you got Clooney is what you got.
你得到了，你得到了克鲁尼的真传。

1189
00:52:03.960 --> 00:52:04.580
I did.
没错。

1190
00:52:04.780 --> 00:52:05.980
One degree of separation.
一度人脉。

1191
00:52:06.340 --> 00:52:09.160
I think that prank just keeps getting cooler like that.
我觉得那个恶作剧因为这样变得越来越酷了。

1192
00:52:09.440 --> 00:52:10.660
That's pretty fancy.
那真是太高级了。

1193
00:52:10.760 --> 00:52:11.460
I think so too.
我也这么觉得。

1194
00:52:11.620 --> 00:52:11.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1195
00:52:11.740 --> 00:52:12.480
That's a good prank.
那是个好恶作剧。

1196
00:52:12.740 --> 00:52:15.260
Let's get into the meat of your interview here, John.
让我们进入你采访的重点吧，约翰。

1197
00:52:15.600 --> 00:52:16.980
I thought we were doing pretty good.
我还以为我们聊得挺好的呢。

1198
00:52:17.240 --> 00:52:19.680
We were, but we should intro you a little.
确实很好，但我们应该先简单介绍一下你。

1199
00:52:19.980 --> 00:52:22.500
John, thank you so much for coming on the show.
约翰，非常感谢你来到我们的节目。

1200
00:52:22.500 --> 00:52:28.300
So we always like to ask our guests a little bit about how they came to be on the office.
我们总是喜欢问嘉宾一些关于他们是如何加入《办公室》的问题。

1201
00:52:28.340 --> 00:52:34.040
And I know you've told this story like a million times, but is it true that you were
我知道你已经讲过这个故事一百万遍了，但传闻是真的吗，你最初

1202
00:52:34.040 --> 00:52:36.160
originally asked to audition for Dwight?
被邀请去试镜德怀特这个角色？

1203
00:52:37.160 --> 00:52:38.300
Yes, I was.
是的，确实如此。

1204
00:52:38.460 --> 00:52:44.340
And that reminds me that about six seasons into the show, someone was like, I love how you say
这让我想起剧集播到第六季左右时，有人跟我说，我喜欢你读

1205
00:52:44.340 --> 00:52:44.740
Dwight.
“德怀特”的方式。

1206
00:52:44.840 --> 00:52:46.560
And I was like, how do you say it?
我说，我是怎么读的？

1207
00:52:46.660 --> 00:52:47.320
And they were like, Dwight.
他们说，德怀特。

1208
00:52:47.440 --> 00:52:48.540
And I was like, I know Dwight.
我说，我知道是德怀特啊。

1209
00:52:48.780 --> 00:52:49.880
And they were like, nope, Dwight.
他们说，不，是德怀特。

1210
00:52:50.480 --> 00:52:52.360
And I was like, no, no, I'm saying it right.
我说，不，不，我读得是对的。

1211
00:52:52.360 --> 00:52:52.940
It's Dwight.
就是德怀特。

1212
00:52:53.100 --> 00:52:54.540
And they were like, nope, it's not.
他们说，不，不对。

1213
00:52:54.840 --> 00:53:01.060
So, um, yes, I auditioned or no, I was offered to come in and audition for the role of Dwight.
所以，嗯，是的，我试镜了，或者说，我被邀请去试镜德怀特这个角色。

1214
00:53:01.200 --> 00:53:02.620
And I was so excited.
我当时特别兴奋。

1215
00:53:02.800 --> 00:53:09.920
I had met, um, Alison Jones randomly out in LA on a general meeting when I had zero dollars
我曾在洛杉矶的一次普通会面上偶然遇到了艾莉森·琼斯，那时我身上

1216
00:53:09.920 --> 00:53:10.420
to my name.
一分钱都没有。

1217
00:53:10.420 --> 00:53:12.780
And she said, something's coming on our first meeting.
在我们的第一次会面上，她说，有个项目要来了。

1218
00:53:12.980 --> 00:53:13.800
Our only meeting.
我们唯一的一次会面。

1219
00:53:13.900 --> 00:53:15.100
She said, something's coming called the office.
她说，有个叫《办公室》的剧要开拍了。

1220
00:53:15.240 --> 00:53:15.780
You'd be great for it.
你很适合这个角色。

1221
00:53:15.860 --> 00:53:16.120
I said, great.
我说，太棒了。

1222
00:53:16.440 --> 00:53:22.020
So then I got back to New York and they said, um, there's this show called the office.
后来我回到纽约，他们说，嗯，有个叫《办公室》的剧。

1223
00:53:22.160 --> 00:53:25.380
And I was like, oh my God, Alison Jones, the greatest human ever told me about this.
我说，天哪，艾莉森·琼斯，那个最棒的人跟我提过这个。

1224
00:53:25.440 --> 00:53:28.600
And, uh, they said, you're going in for the role of Dwight.
然后，呃，他们说，你要去试镜德怀特这个角色。

1225
00:53:28.700 --> 00:53:30.720
And I had been a huge fan of the British show.
我当时是英版剧集的超级粉丝。

1226
00:53:30.820 --> 00:53:35.580
And I was like, I don't know, man, that's, that's not, I don't know if I'm right for that
我就说，我不知道，伙计，那，那不是，我不知道我是否适合那个

1227
00:53:35.580 --> 00:53:35.920
role.
角色。

1228
00:53:35.920 --> 00:53:39.660
And so I weirdly have no idea what I was thinking.
说来奇怪，我当时脑子里在想什么，我自己都不知道。

1229
00:53:39.660 --> 00:53:41.540
I said, um, you know what?
我说，嗯，你知道吗？

1230
00:53:41.680 --> 00:53:43.760
I read the pilot and I said, you know what?
我读了试播集的剧本，然后我说，你知道吗？

1231
00:53:43.760 --> 00:53:44.920
I'm going to put my best foot forward.
我要全力以赴。

1232
00:53:45.100 --> 00:53:46.740
Let me know when they're casting Jim's.
等他们开始选吉姆这个角色时再通知我吧。

1233
00:53:46.900 --> 00:53:52.100
And I remember the response from the NBC casting director to my manager at the time was no, but
我记得当时NBC选角导演给我的经纪人的回复是：不，说实话，他以为他是谁啊，竟然放弃试镜，放弃试镜的机会。

1234
00:53:52.100 --> 00:53:57.140
honestly, who does he think he is like passing up an audition, an opportunity to audition.
而且，说实话，他以为他是谁啊，竟然放弃试镜，放弃试镜的机会。

1235
00:53:57.320 --> 00:53:59.360
And lo and behold, I thought it was over.
结果没想到，我以为一切都结束了。

1236
00:53:59.520 --> 00:54:04.280
And I think it was like five, six weeks later that they called and they were like, all right,
大概过了五六周吧，他们打电话来说，好了，

1237
00:54:04.280 --> 00:54:06.500
they're looking for Jim's now and they'll have you back.
他们现在在找吉姆的人选了，会让你回来试镜的。

1238
00:54:07.640 --> 00:54:09.820
And then my gosh, that's so crazy.
天哪，那真是太疯狂了。

1239
00:54:10.020 --> 00:54:15.120
And then when we finally did our screen test, you, you were living in New York and you had
后来当我们最终进行试镜时，你，你当时住在纽约，你不得不

1240
00:54:15.120 --> 00:54:21.880
to fly to LA for that screen test with all these New Yorkers that were auditioning, which
飞到洛杉矶参加试镜，和所有那些参加试镜的纽约人一起，那

1241
